    <!-- Real-time event reaction bark templates for wom_reaction.script.
         Delivered as PDA messages the moment ALifePlus records a high-signal event
         on the current level, attributed to a nearby non-combat stalker.

         Key format: st_wom_reaction_{consequence_suffix}_{NNN}
                     st_wom_reaction_{category}_{NNN}     (category-level fallback)
                     st_wom_reaction_generic_{NNN}         (catch-all)
         One is picked at random; variants referencing a slot whose value is empty
         are filtered out by pick_dialogue_variant's gated_tokens before selection,
         so every pool must include at least one location-free line as a fallback.

         Tone: present-tense, radio-chatter style — the speaker just heard this
         through their earpiece or PDA feed, a moment ago.

         Available slots (same as area-recap event templates):
           #location#           — smart terrain display name (gated when absent)
           #some_members_subject#  — e.g. "some Loners", "a Duty patrol"
           #a_squad_subject#       — e.g. "a Loner crew", "a Duty unit"
           #a_member_subject#      — e.g. "a Loner", "a Duty soldier"
           #plural_subject#        — e.g. "Loners", "Duty soldiers"
           #some_members_other#    — same forms for the other party
           #a_squad_other#
           #a_member_other#
           #plural_other#
           #kills#              — word form of kill count (e.g. "three", "a")
           #count_other#        — e.g. "four Bandits", "some Mercs" -->

